 opean double bass soloist Dominik Wagner. Liu was awarded a collaborative
  piano fellowship at the Bowdoin International Music Festival in Brunswic
 k\, Maine\, in the summer of 2025. This summer\, he joins the IU Summer S
 tring Academy as a faculty collaborative pianist. Liu began to study pian
 o professionally with Ling Gao at age nine. At age 12\, he was admitted t
 o the Affiliated Middle School of Sichuan Conservatory of Music (China) w
 ith the first-place score. He studied with Chenggang Yang\, graduated as 
 the first-place student\, and acquired his high school diploma there. He 
 earned his Bachelor of Music degree from the School of Music at The Unive
 rsity of Kansas in 2019. He continued his Master of Music study there as 
 a teaching assistant and studied with Scott McBride Smith and Eric Zuber.
  In May 2024\, he completed a Graduate Artist Certificate as a teaching f
 ellow at the University of North Texas\, studying with Vladimir Viardo.</
